<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Train H ~ the hosted road

!! Contents

* [[Ground and crew|#/ground]] · [[Commit walk|#/walk]] · [[Witness and red window|#/witness]] · [[Collision sheet|#/collisions]] · [[Done when|#/done]] · [[Rulings|#/rulings]].

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/ground`>>

!! Ground and crew

Start pure signed-act and grant vectors beside N and W on disjoint files. Start the live cut after N hands over the joint AID and W hands over gate sorting. One authority lead owns `hosting.ts` and `hosting-store.ts` through one coordinated signed-byte re-cut. A store builder owns HOT row persistence; a door builder owns introduction, answer and strangers' dial. The operator's seat signs ONE delegation to a hosting key. That key signs every hosting act and seeds every epoch. The delegation persists across sessions. A session wearing another face signs nothing for the hearth. The worn face hosts and walks; a vessel wearing none does neither.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/walk`>>

!! Commit walk

# ''SPECIFIED: authority and dials.'' `hosting-delegation.ts` carries H2's delegation, hosting key and three dials; its named red reads unskipped. The live issuer and reader still need the same signed shape. Their cut verifies the seat, delegation, key, Nexus, epoch parent and each dial; the hosting key seeds each epoch across session endings.
# ''SPECIFIED: H8 grant.'' `walker-grant.ts` signs the grant and verifies under a public half; its named red reads unskipped. The serving rows and live cut remain owed. Derive the public halves for serving rows during the hosting-act re-cut; a SERVING checker holds no minting secret.
# ''LIVE: one signed-byte cut.'' Move issuer, reader, hosting store and socket sorter together. Preserve each spend as one sealed HOT row and each roll as one committed state row. Re-derive hosting-doc acts from committed state. A row that refuses to open refuses by name. Keep the floor sorter free of hosting rows.
# ''LIVE: introduction and answer.'' A token buys a knock. Only the operator's answer or a pre-answer gives standing. A walker's invitation vests at the host's next roll; a host invitation receives floor 1 at once. Wire the strangers' three-dial decision and the host door. Fold H7 invite canon after the live reader passes.
# ''GATE: E's walker arm.'' Prove a SERVING hearth checks the walker grant with its public half and no minting secret in its serving tier. Only then arm E's walker path.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/witness`>>

!! Witness and red window

`HOSTING_ACT_BINDS_OPERATOR_SEAT_AND_THREE_DIALS` and `SERVING_CHECKS_WALKER_GRANT_WITH_PUBLIC_HALF` read unskipped for the pure modules. A signed-byte change can redden issuer, reader, store and sorter together; one commit moves their fixtures and consumers. Prove that a token alone grants no standing, an answer or pre-answer grants exactly the intended class, and all three dials survive roll and restart. Run the grant verifier under a serving view that holds no minting secret.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/collisions`>>

!! Collision sheet

| Seam | H hand-off |
|---|---|
| N | Consume final AID and operator seat from N; leave charter and cofounding bytes with N. |
| W | Take `socket-sorter.ts` after W's gate cutover; keep its verified face and per-Nexus gate pin. |
| S8 and sealed-store step 3 | Keep hosting HOT rows under S key and serving rows under SK; leave selves rows and Repo value sealing to their owners. |
| O1 | Consume the worn session face through O1's verified session. A delegated hosting key, rather than the session lifetime, sustains acts. |
| E and X | E waits for H8's public-half verifier before its walker arm. X consumes hosted restart and strangers' dial without changing H's act image. |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/done`>>

!! Done when

A standing operator-seat delegation authorizes one hosting key. That key signs every act and seeds each epoch. A worn face hosts and walks within that delegation. Each act binds three dials, and their decisions survive roll and restart. A token buys a knock; only an answer or pre-answer grants standing. The SERVING tier verifies walker grants through public halves alone, and E's walker arm passes that gate.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/rulings`>>

!! Rulings

The hosting-key and worn-face rulings already stand at the roadmap's `#/rulings` (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/rulings`>>). Its H path names the one re-cut, answer door, three dials and H8 (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-road`>>; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/the-loops`>>). Flag a proposed signer only when it departs from that delegation. E's walker arm waits on H8's public-half check.

<<~/ahu>>

